WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Long before they were written
down, the oldest Hindu scriptures,

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:08.300
the Vedas, were passed on by
memory, for many centuries.

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.540
Reciters learned memory techniques
that preserve every sound.

4
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.230
Yet there is no one book
that all Hindus share,

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.230
and no one leader for all Hindus.

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.980
So where does authority come from?

7
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.870
In this mission, you'll
explore Hindu scriptures,

8
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.730
from ancient hymns to much-loved
epics, and how they are used today.

9
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.000
Then you'll meet two great
teachers, Shankara and Ramanuja,

10
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.590
who drew very different
ideas from the same texts.

11
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: find out where
Hindus look for authority, and why.
